oss":"they"}],"gloss":"they"},{"surface":"இரந்து","parts":[{"text":"இரந்து","lemma":"இரந்து","gloss":"begging"}],"gloss":"begging","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உண்ணும்","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"உண்","gloss":"eat/drink"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"that eats"}],"gloss":"drinking"},{"surface":"அளவை","parts":[{"text":"அளவு","lemma":"அளவு","gloss":"measure/state"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"particle"}],"gloss":"such a state"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈன்மரோ","parts":[{"text":"ஈன்","lemma":"ஈன்","gloss":"give birth"},{"text":"மர்","lemma":"மர்","gloss":"they"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"interrogative"}],"gloss":"will they give birth?"},{"surface":"இவ்","parts":[{"text":"இவ்","lemma":"இவ்","gloss":"this"}],"gloss":"this","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உலகத்தானே","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்தானே","lemma":"உலகத்தானே","gloss":"in this world"}],"gloss":"in this world","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Even if an infant dies, or even if a lump of flesh is born, / saying 'this is not a man', they do not fail to cleave it with a sword. / Chained like a dog, put in distress and confined, / the little water offered as charity by unfriendly foes, / without fortitude, to quench the fire of the stomach, / they themselves begging and drinking, in such a state, / will mothers give birth to them in this world?","translation":"Even if an infant is born dead, or if it is but a lifeless lump of flesh, warriors do not fail to cleave it with a sword, declaring, 'This is no man!' Yet, to quench the burning fire of the stomach, without any pride, begging and drinking the little water offered as charity by unfriendly captors who have chained and confined them like a dog in misery—will mothers in this world ever give birth to such men?","modern":"ஒரு குழந்தை பிறந்து இறந்தாலும், அல்லது வெறும் தசைப்பிண்டமாகப் பிறந்தாலும், 'இது ஆண்மகன் அல்ல' என்று கூறி அதனை வாளால் கீறி அடக்கம் செய்யத் தவற மாட்டார்கள் வீரர்கள். ஆனால், சங்கிலியால் பிணைக்கப்பட்ட நாயைப் போலத் துன்புறுத்திச் சிறையில் அடைத்த பகைவர்கள் இடும் பிச்சையாகிய சிறுதண்ணீரை, மானம் இல்லாமல் தன் வயிற்றுப் பசியைத் தணிப்பதற்காகத் தானே இரந்து குடிக்கும் இழிவான நிலையில் வாழும் மக்களை, இந்த உலகத்தில் உள்ள தாய்மார்கள் பெற்றெடுப்பார்களா?","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the Chera king Kanaikkal Irumporai when he was imprisoned by his rival, the Chola king Sengkannan. Suffering from intense thirst in prison, the king asked the guards for water, but they delayed bringing it, treating him with contempt. When they finally brought it, the king felt deeply humiliated to accept water given as charity by his captors, comparing his state to that of a chained dog. He reflects on the ancient warrior code where even stillborn infants or formless lumps of flesh were ceremonially cut with a sword to ensure they died as warriors. He questions whether mothers in this world would ever proudly give birth to men who survive on the charity of their enemies, choosing death over dishonor. The key words are 'வாளின் தப்பார்' (they do not fail to cleave with a sword) and 'மதுகை இன்றி' (without fortitude/pride).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.25],[0.25,0.76],[0.76,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,3.0],[3.0,3.2],[3.2,3.6],[3.6,4.0],[4.0,4.56],[4.56,5.08],[5.08,5.51],[5.51,6.2],[6.2,6.8],[6.8,7.65],[7.65,8.5],[8.5,8.9],[8.9,9.3],[9.3,10.5],[10.5,10.7],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,11.5],[11.5,11.9],[11.9,12.2],[12.2,12.8],[12.8,13.4],[13.4,13.7],[13.7,14.3],[14.3,14.9],[14.9,15.2],[15.4,15.6],[15.6,15.9]],"female":[[0.0,0.3],[0.3,0.9],[0.9,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,3.3],[3.3,3.5],[3.5,3.95],[3.95,4.4],[4.4,4.96],[4.96,5.49],[5.49,5.94],[5.94,6.65],[6.65,7.0],[7.0,7.85],[7.85,8.7],[8.7,9.1],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,10.8],[10.8,11.0],[11.0,11.3],[11.3,12.0],[12.0,12.4],[12.4,12.64],[12.64,13.12],[13.12,13.6],[13.6,13.9],[14.2,14.8],[14.8,15.1],[15.1,15.32],[15.32,15.77],[15.77,16.0]]},"sync":[[["குழவி","infant"]],[["இறப்பினும்","even if [it] dies"]],[["ஊன்தடி","lump of flesh"]],[["பிறப்பினும்","even if [it] is born"]]